le we scale up clean energy. Abandoning it prematurely could lead to energy shortages, higher prices, and economic hardship. Finally, the debate isn’t binary. We can develop unconventional oil resources while simultaneously investing in renewables, efficiency, and environmental safeguards. Responsible regulation, industry best practices, and public oversight can minimize harm. Given the pressing need for reliable, affordable energy today, the development of unconventional oil is a pragmatic and justified choice.
